item.description:
For the period from October 1st 2019 to July 12th 2025, relating to collections of audio recordings and textual material which contain any of the following:
- Aboriginal (Indigenous, First Nations, Métis, Inuit) music played upon a Violin/Fiddle;
- Métis dance;
- Métis song or music using other instruments;

We request digital/digitised copies of relevant policy documents (please include both draft and final versions):
- Museum policies affecting any barriers to access for these collections.
- Museum policies around Indigenous access to collections of Indigenous material in the collections (without repatriation). 
- Museum policies regarding repatriation.
- All Museum policies, protocols and guidelines related to UNDRIP that inform access to and repatriation from Indigenous collections.

Please include both policies in effect and policies under development. | 24 pages | Source: Canadian Museum of History

